episode 4 of hawkeye has landed and the  series is proving yet again that it can  bring the drama and the fun on a much  smaller scale than big budget mcu  properties the show is doing a fantastic  job of building the relationship between  clint and kate who had some very high  highs and very low lows this week this  week's installment was all about clint  and kate's partnership which the former  eventually seems to surrender to after  three episodes of hesitation kate has  been pushing for their team status from  the get-go and things were finally  starting to go her way until the ending  that is the episode picks up with  eleanor and jack catching clint and kate  in the penthouse and the foursome sits  down and has a rather awkward chat after  admitting that he's working with kate  clint leaves and is warned by eleanor to  take it easy with her daughter since  tragedy seems to follow him after he  leaves she calls someone on the phone  and leaves a message saying she needs to  talk about something urgent who is she  talking to our guest is kingpin who did  not show up in this episode despite many  rumors suggesting he'd make an  appearance in a post-credit scene  eleanor's phone call is just another  tease at the looming threat and hawkeye  after three episodes worth of red  herrings the mention of uncle in episode  3 got the kingpin buzz going especially  after we saw a mystery man pinch young  echo's cheek the mystery phone call is  not to jack since he was in the  penthouse at the time and ekko and kazi  are both unlikely candidates this phone  call was probably for someone we haven't  seen yet in the show and all signs are  pointing to kingpin aka wilson fisk but  we are all impatiently waiting to see in  his broad shoulder glory  after he leaves kate's penthouse clint  makes a phone call to the most  understanding woman in the world to tell  her he's going to need another day laura  is as sympathetic to the cause as she's  always been but something different  about the couple's conversation is worth  a second look she's already been doing  some detective work for clint after he  texted her some info on sloane limited  after recovering his ronin sword and  laura seems to have some skills we've  never been privy to laura lets clint  know that jack is the ceo of sloan  limited and it only took her mere  minutes to come up with this information  how is she researching and getting  answers so quickly has she just picked  up research skills from her husband over  the years probably not and here's why  swapping english for german to confuse  her kids laura asked clint if anything  else went missing from the avengers  compound he immediately knows she's  talking about the rolex which we saw at  the auction in episode 1 and says he  thought it was destroyed years ago laura  agrees but then says she felt the same  way about the ronin suit clint decides  to look into it and we get the sense  that this rolex is connected to laura  somehow she seems very concerned that it  could be in the wrong hands and the  episode turns to a recovery mission of  the stolen watch signs suggest that  laura might have a secret history  especially after clint tells kate the  person connected to the watch has been  quote out of the game for a long time  was laura a former shield agent is that  how she met clint some fans on twitter  are suggesting laura is mockingbird  hawkeye's ex-wife but current girlfriend  from the comics it's a lot to unpack but  hopefully we'll get more on that in  future episodes when clint and kate's  mission turns toward the rolex they  track it to a mysterious apartment kate  gets herself inside and finds a watch  reasonably quickly but it's also sitting  next to a notebook with the names and  ages of clint's family on it in the  middle of the recovery clint deduces  that cade is in echo's apartment after  realizing the mysterious strobe lights  are a silent alarm  kate is then surprised by ekko and the  two begin to fight in the apartment  while clint is on the nearby rooftop  also being attacked by someone he thinks  is echo the foursome all end up together  on the rooftop and a well-choreographed  group fight ensues clint's assailant is  fully masked and remains a mystery to  him and us until the end we get this  sense he has an idea of who he's  fighting based on their attack style and  weapons used and the big reveal happens  just before the episode ends elena  belova last seen in black widow has made  her way to new york and seems hell-bent  on taking out clint as vengeance for the  death of natasha after her mask is off  she escapes by launching herself off the  building and has gone into the night  it's here that there is a rift in the  relationship between kate and clint as  he declares they are not partners and  never were clint informs kate that  someone has hired a black widow assassin  and he's going solo he's gotten very  real  very quickly  the appearance of a black widow has  brought out the grief in him yet again  and this debacle is now so much more  than squashing the ronin identity  however he does not appear to know that  this is elena did not even tell him  about her adoptive sister there are so  many unanswered questions but hopefully  we'll get some clarity in episode 5.  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  hawkeye are coming soon subscribe to our  youtube channel and hit the bell so you  don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

